          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original reference is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"}> Nathan Seiberg
              ,
              %em
                New theories in six dimensions and matrix description of M-theory on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^5
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 5
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^5/\mathbb{Z}_2
              Phys. Lett. B408 (1997) 98–104 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705221"}> arXiv:hep-th/9705221
              )
          %p Review is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ofer+Aharony"}> Ofer Aharony
                ,
                %em A brief review of “little string theories”
                , Class. Quant. Grav. 17 (2000) 929–938,
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911147"}> arXiv:hep-th/9911147
                ).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kutasov"}> David Kutasov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Little String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://users.ictp.it/~pub_off/lectures/lns007/Kutasov/Kutasov.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Little string theories on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = (1,0)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %ul
            %li
              E. Gava, K.S. Narain, M.H. Sarmadi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Little String Theories in Heterotic Backgrounds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0112200"} arXiv:hep-th/0112200
          %p
            and via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            methods:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Del+Zotto"}> Michele Del Zotto
              , Muyang Liu, Paul-Konstantin Oehlmann,
              %em 6D Heterotic Little String Theories and F-theory Geometry: An Introduction
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.13502"}> arXiv:2303.13502
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            between type IIA and type IIB little strings is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Jungmin Kim, Seok Kim, Kimyeong Lee,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Little strings and T-duality
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.07277"} arXiv:1503.07277
          %p
            Construction within
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Lakshya Bhardwaj,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Del+Zotto"} Michele Del Zotto
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"} Jonathan Heckman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"} David Morrison
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Rudelius"} Tom Rudelius
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
              %em F-theory and the Classification of Little Strings
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1511.05565"}> arXiv:1511.05565
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mina+Aganagic"}> Mina Aganagic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some mathematical applications of little string theory
                %a{:href => "http://ymsc.tsinghua.edu.cn:8090/strings/"} Strings 2016
                (
                %a{:href => "http://ymsc.tsinghua.edu.cn:8090/strings/slides/8.1/Aganagic%20v2.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Joonho Kim, Kimyeong Lee,
                %em
                  Little strings on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_n
                  orbifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03116"}> arXiv:1702.03116
                )
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theories"} D=3 N=4 super Yang-Mills theories
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} compact hyperkähler manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coulomb+branches"} Coulomb branches
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+string+theories"} little string theories
          %ul
            %li#Intriligator99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Intriligator"}> Kenneth Intriligator
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Compactified Little String Theories and Compact Moduli Spaces of Vacua
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9909219"} arXiv:hep-th/9909219
          %p
            Relation of little string theory to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} quantum geometric Langlands correspondence
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#AganagicFrenkelOkounkov17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mina+Aganagic"}> Mina Aganagic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"} Edward Frenkel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Okounkov"} Andrei Okounkov
              %em
                Quantum
                = succeed "-Langlands" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.03146"}> arXiv:1701.03146
              )
          %p also
          %ul
            %li
              Babak Haghighat, Rui Sun,
              %em M5 branes and Theta Functions
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.04938"}> arXiv:1811.04938
              )
          %p
            Discussion with emphasis on terminology from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Del+Zotto"}> Michele Del Zotto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kantaro+Ohmori"} Kantaro Ohmori
              = succeed "," do
                %em 2-Group Symmetries of 6D Little String Theories and T-Duality
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03489"} arXiv:2009.03489
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00023-021-01018-3"}> doi:10.1007/s00023-021-01018-3
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Andrea Dei,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+J.+Martinec"} Emil J. Martinec
              %em On the string theory of a single NS5-brane
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.22300"}> arXiv:2506.22300
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#open_dbrane_theories
            Open D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-brane theories
          %p
            For light
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            ending on NS5-branes (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "NS5-brane#DBranesEndingOnNS5Branes"} there
          %ul
            %li#GopakumarMinwallaSeibergStrominger00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rajesh+Gopakumar"}> Rajesh Gopakumar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shiraz+Minwalla"} Shiraz Minwalla
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"} Nathan Seiberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"} Andrew Strominger
                = succeed "," do
                  %em OM Theory in Diverse Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0006062"} arXiv:hep-th/0006062
            %li#Harmark00
              %p
                Troels Harmark,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Open Branes in Space-Time Non-Commutative Little String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0007147"} arXiv:hep-th/0007147
            %li#Lu06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jian+Xin+Lu"}> Jian Xin Lu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 + p)
                    \-Dimensional Open
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(p - 2)
                    Brane Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0102056"} arXiv:hep-th/0102056
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2001/08/049"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2001/08/049
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Dan Israel, Ari Pakman, Jan Troost,
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-branes in Little String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0502073"} arXiv:hep-th/0502073
          %h3#via_the_plane_wave_matrix_model Via the plane wave matrix model
          %p
            On a double-scaling limit of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            in which aspects of little string theory become visible:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hai+Lin"}> Hai Lin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"} Juan Maldacena
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fivebranes from gauge theory
                %strong 74
                084014 (2006) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0509235"}> arXiv:hep-th/0509235
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.74.084014"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.74.084014
            %li
              %p
                Henry Ling, Ali Reza Mohazab, Hsien-Hang Shieh, Greg van Anders,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"} Mark Van Raamsdonk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Little String Theory from a Double-Scaled Matrix Model
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0606014"} arXiv:hep-th/0606014
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2006/10/018"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2006/10/018
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuhma+Asano"}> Yuhma Asano
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goro+Ishiki"} Goro Ishiki
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takaki+Matsumoto"} Takaki Matsumoto
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinji+Shimasaki"} Shinji Shimasaki
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiromasa+Watanabe"} Hiromasa Watanabe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the existence of the NS5-brane limit of the plane wave matrix model
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.13716"} arXiv:2211.13716
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/ptep/ptad042"} doi:10.1093/ptep/ptad042
